    <h2>
        <a id="basics" class="anchor" href="#basics" aria-hidden="true"></a>Audit Logging Mechanism
    </h2>
    <p>
        The audit logging mechanism checks whether audit logging is enabled via the DisableAudit setting from
        <code>AuditLogSettings</code>.

        If audit logging is not disabled, it proceeds to set up the necessary configurations.
    </p>

    <h4>Audit Log Settings:</h4>
    <ul class="in-content-list">
        <li>The connection string for the database (<code>auditConnectionString</code>) is retrieved from <code>AuditLogSettings.ConnectionString</code>.</li>
        <li>The global enrich options are configured to include the <code>ApplicationId</code>, <code>ApplicationName</code> and <code>ApplicationVersion</code> from the application's configuration and environment helpers.</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>Audit Database Settings:</h4>
    <ul class="in-content-list">
        <li>The database connection string, schema name, severity level, and table name for storing audit logs are set from the configuration options (<code>AuditLogSettings</code>).</li>
        <li>The severity level for the audit log is defined as an enumeration <code>AuditLogSeverity</code>, which is set to the value from the configuration (<code>Severity</code>), e.g., <code>"Verbose"</code>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>Adding Audit Services:</h4>
    <p>The <code>AddSqlServerSerilogAudit</code> method is called to configure SQL Server-based audit logging using Serilog. It is passed the audit settings and global enrich options to initialize the logging mechanism.</p>
    <pre><code>
                    #region Audit


                    if (Settings.Instance.AuditLogSettings.DisableAudit == false)
                    {
                        Log.Information("Configuring Audit Log...");

                        string auditConnectionString = Settings.Instance.AuditLogSettings.ConnectionString;

                        GlobalEnrichOptions globalEnrichOptions = new GlobalEnrichOptions()
                        {
                            ApplicationId = ApplicationId = Settings.Instance.AppSettings.ApplicationId,
                            ApplicationName = EnvironmentHelper.ApplicationName,
                            ApplicationVersion = EnvironmentHelper.Version
                        };

                        AuditDbSettings settings = new AuditDbSettings()
                        {
                            ConnectionString = auditConnectionString, 
                            DisableAudit = Settings.Instance.AuditLogSettings.DisableAudit, 
                            SchemaName = Settings.Instance.AuditLogSettings.SchemaName,
                            Severity = (AuditLogSeverity)Settings.Instance.AuditLogSettings.Severity,
                            TableName = Settings.Instance.AuditLogSettings.TableName
                        };

                        builder.Services.AddSqlServerSerilogAudit(settings, globalEnrichOptions);

                    }

                     #endregion
                </code></pre>
    <h4>Configuration:</h4>
    <p>The settings for the audit log are specified in a configuration file (<code>appsettings.json</code>):</p>
    <pre><code>
                    "AuditLogSettings": {
                        "DisableAudit": false,
                        "ConnectionString": "Server=hubp1-tdw-db2o;Database=DCCMeter_dev;Trusted_Connection=True;Integrated Security=true;TrustServerCertificate=True;",
                        "TableName": "AuditLog",
                        "SchemaName": "logs",
                        "Severity": "Verbose"
                    }
                </code></pre>

    <h5>Settings Explained:</h5>
    <ul class="in-content-list">
        <li><strong>DisableAudit:</strong> Determines whether audit logging is enabled or not.</li>
        <li><strong>ConnectionString:</strong> Specifies the database connection string.</li>
        <li><strong>TableName:</strong> Defines the table name for storing audit logs.</li>
        <li><strong>SchemaName:</strong> Defines the schema where the audit logs will be stored.</li>
        <li><strong>Severity:</strong> Sets the level of logging (e.g., <code>"Verbose"</code> for detailed logs).</li>
    </ul>

    <p>This setup ensures that audit logs are securely stored in a SQL Server database, with enriched application context and customizable logging severity.</p>

    <h2>
        <a id="attribute" class="anchor" href="attribute" aria-hidden="true"></a>Controller setup
    </h2>
    <p>
        In the controller, the <span><code>[Audit]</code></span> attribute is used to log actions for tracking purposes.

        If logging is needed only for certain methods within controller then attribute <span><code>[Audit]</code></span> should be written above those methods.
    </p>
    <h2>
        <a id="dependencies" class="anchor" href="#dependencies" aria-hidden="true"></a>Dependecies
    </h2>
    <p>
        In order for Audit to work, we need to use classes from other projects.
        We will do this by adding these projects to the dependencies as follows:
        <ul>
            <li>1. Right-click on the DccMeter.API project &rarr; <strong>Add</strong> &rarr; <strong>Project References</strong></li>
            <li>2. Select the project we want to add as a dependency</li>
            <li>3. Click <strong>OK</strong></li>
        </ul>
    </p>
    <p>
        The projects that need to be added to the dependency are:
        <ul>
            <li><p><code>Euronet.System</code></p></li>
            <li><p><code>Euronet.Audit</code></li>
            <li><p><code>Euronet.Audit.Serilog.SqlServer</code></p></li>
            <li><p><code>Euronet.Audit.Api.Domain</code></p></li>
        </ul>
    </p>
    <p>
        The listed projects also depend on each other so that:
        <ul>
            <li><p><code>Euronet.Audit</code> project depends on <code>Euronet.System</code> so in project Euronet.Audit need to add Euronet.System in dependencies </p></li>
            <li><p><code>Euronet.Audit.Serilog.SqlServer</code> depends on <code>Euronet.System</code>, <code>Euronet.Audit</code> so in project Euronet.Audit.Serilog.SqlServer need to add Euronet.System, Euronet.Audit in dependencies</p></li>
        </ul>
    </p>

</div>
